{
    "_README": [
        "Static tide & tidal-stream data for Dublin Bay / Dún Laoghaire.",
        "",
        "events:",
        "  HW/LW times and heights for Dún Laoghaire pier.",
        "  Source: tides4fishing.com/ie/leinster/dun-laoghaire (May 2026).",
        "  Times are LOCAL Europe/Dublin (currently IST, UTC+1).",
        "  Heights in metres (MLLW reference).",
        "  Refresh from the same source (or Admiralty EasyTide) every",
        "  ~7 days; the app silently hides the tide UI once events go stale.",
        "",
        "defaultTideRose:",
        "  Best-effort approximation, NOT verbatim NP218.",
        "  Based on the well-documented Dublin Bay tidal-stream pattern:",
        "    - weak streams (~0.3 kn neaps, ~0.5 kn springs central bay)",
        "    - flood sets ~N (350–010°T), peak around HW-3",
        "    - ebb  sets ~S (180–195°T), peak around HW+3",
        "    - slack near HW and near LW",
        "  Sources used: Irish Cruising Club Directions for the East and",
        "  North Coasts of Ireland, Reed's Nautical Almanac, and the",
        "  standard semi-diurnal pattern for the western Irish Sea.",
        "  Values are SPRING rates; the engine does not yet de-rate for",
        "  neaps, so figures are kept conservative. Sanity-check against",
        "  Admiralty NP218 (Tidal Stream Atlas: Irish Sea) before relying",
        "  on them tactically. To suppress arrows entirely, replace the",
        "  array with [].",
        "",
        "marksTideRose:",
        "  Per-mark overrides for spots where local knowledge says the",
        "  stream differs from the central-bay default (e.g. accelerated",
        "  through Dalkey Sound, eddy at the Pier Heads, stronger over",
        "  Burford Bank). Empty until verified by an experienced local.",
        "",
        "SCHEMA",
        "------",
        "events[]: each = {",
        "    datetime: 'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM',     local Europe/Dublin time",
        "    type:     'high' | 'low',",
        "    height_m: number                  metres above chart datum",
        "}",
        "",
        "defaultTideRose[]: 13 entries, h = -6..+6 hours from HW.",
        "Each entry = { h: int, set: 0..359 deg true, drift: knots }.",
        "",
        "marksTideRose: { 'A': [ ...13 entries... ], 'B': [ ... ] }"
    ],
